two of the country's most famous  military units are under intense  scrutiny today over troubling incidents  on opposite sides of the world a human  smuggling investigation led to the mass  arrests of 16 Marines from the first  Marine Division yesterday at Camp  Pendleton in California two other  Marines were arrested and charged  earlier this month now the accusations  range from smuggling illegal immigrants  into the country to drug-related  offenses and in a separate case an  entire platoon of elite Navy SEALs was  sent home from Iraq over allegations of  sexual misconduct and drinking while  deployed Jamie yuccas is at Camp  Pendleton that's north of San Diego  Jamie what more do we know well this is  what we know right now Tony those 16  Marines are in the brig on the base and  authorities here say they've already  questioned eight additional Marines  Marines are known for their discipline  and dedication to country but in the  past month authorities here have  arrested 18 Marines from this base some  for allegedly helping ferry undocumented  immigrants into this country in exchange  for money  [Music]  Thursday's arrest of 16 Marines occurred  in dramatic fashion in front of their  own entire unit the release of this  information was really so we could be  completely transparent the Marines were  made to line up in morning formation  like this one the Marine Corps filmed  earlier at California's Camp Pendleton  they were then arrested for offenses  that range from human smuggling to drug  related activities all 16 suspects are  members of the oldest active duty marine  division headquartered here just 60  miles north of the Mexican border  none of the Marines were among the 66  hundred active duty and National Guard  troops assigned to bolster border patrol  at the southwestern border the Marines  say Thursday's arrests stem from an  earlier arrest of two more Camp  Pendleton Marines near the Mexican  border in early July the pair were  pulled over with three 